            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for to grow weak, then the Arabic for to bleed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: أرق",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أرق — araq — \"insomnia\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عانى أبي من الأرق قبل السفر. ʿānā abī min al-araq qabla as-safar. My father suffered from insomnia before the trip."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Do not mix it up with عرق, ʿaraq, sweat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أرق (araq) is built on the native Arabic root ʾ-r-q, \"to be sleepless\" (Lane). Araq is sleeplessness at night."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
